    {
      "id": "claim_bc7ffa2a2bba40d0a1d3c6cee05810d3",
      "statement": "The M1 rotation-cascade gate: a failed request whose wire Authorization token differs from the current store token triggers no new refresh (a prior rotation completed — refreshing would burn the just-minted JWT); a straggler arriving during a pending rotation joins that in-flight refresh and replays only after it settles.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/lib/api-client-refresh.ts#L66-L87",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:27be30d0acbac8bc926363156e1fbcbce4eef07d36385d4f88ee316629eb0955:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_27398ebe45af43c880d564151493c2c8",
      "statement": "Reactive 401 recovery replays the original request exactly once with authToken dropped (so a revoked initiating override cannot ride again) and a private replay flag of false; a replay that 401s again surfaces the original ApiError, and the private flag always wins over the public allowReactiveRefresh option, which can never re-enable refresh mid-recovery.",
      "evidence": [
